+        # Make the exported layer's up axis agree with the sim stage's.
+        #
+        # Referencing a layer whose upAxis disagrees with the stage's makes Kit's metrics assembler
+        # compensate by APPENDING a rotation to the referencing prim's xformOpOrder:
+        #
+        #     xformOpOrder = [xformOp:translate, xformOp:orient, xformOp:scale,
+        #                     xformOp:rotateX:unitsResolve]        # the last one being Rx(+90)
+        #
+        # Every pose setter in OmniGibson writes only xformOp:translate and xformOp:orient, and
+        # XFormPrim._set_xform_properties strips only the UNSUFFIXED rotate*/transform ops, so that
+        # trailing op is invisible to all of them while silently post-multiplying every pose they
+        # set: set_position_orientation(orientation=Q) leaves the prim at Q * Rx(90).
+        #
+        # And it is applied INCONSISTENTLY, which is what makes it a correctness bug rather than a
+        # convention. Measured on REALM's impact_drawer cabinet.usd (upAxis=Y; the stage is Z) at
+        # num_envs=2: scene 0's copy of the asset got the resolve op and scene 1's did not -- the
+        # assembler's UnitsAdjust layer is content-hash keyed and only materialized for the first
+        # reference. Same asset, same commanded pose, and the cabinet stood upright in scene 1 while
+        # lying on its back in scene 0, where its drawers then slid vertically and jammed against the
+        # floor at 0.229 m of a 0.300 m range instead of closing.
+        #
+        # So leave the assembler nothing to do. This rotates NOTHING: the up axis is layer metadata,
+        # every caller places the object explicitly afterwards, and for the Z-up assets in the
+        # BEHAVIOR dataset the two axes already agree and this is a no-op.
+        stage_up_axis = (
+            lazy.pxr.UsdGeom.GetStageUpAxis(og.sim.stage)
+            if og.sim is not None
+            else lazy.pxr.UsdGeom.Tokens.z
+        )
+        if lazy.pxr.UsdGeom.GetStageUpAxis(stage) != stage_up_axis:
+            lazy.pxr.UsdGeom.SetStageUpAxis(stage, stage_up_axis)
+
         # Export to a temp file
